      "worked": "Only Mary is correct.\n\nFor Bob, $\\log_2(x)$ requires $x>0$, so\n$$\\begin{align*}2^{\\log_2(x)}&=x\\qquad(x>0).\\end{align*}$$\nHis graph is the part of $y=x$ with $x>0$, excluding the origin.\n\nFor Mary, $2^x>0$ for every real $x$, so\n$$\\begin{align*}\\log_2(2^x)&=x\\qquad(x\\in\\mathbb{R}).\\end{align*}$$\nHer graph is the entire line $y=x$.",
